        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4f8a4404-5913-5d72-a732-b7123866795d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Oakland Raiders, Las Vegas Raiders, National Football League, UNLV Rebels, University of Nevada, Las Vegas\n- People: Mark Davis\n- Places: Oakland, California, Las Vegas, Nevada, Paradise, Nevada\n- Projects: Oakland Raiders relocation to Las Vegas\n- Products: Las Vegas Stadium, Sam Boyd Stadium\n\nFacts:\n- Mark Davis led a successful effort to relocate the Oakland Raiders from Oakland, California to Las Vegas, Nevada.\n- The team was scheduled to begin play as the Las Vegas Raiders in the 2020 NFL season.\n- The relocation could have happened as soon as 2019 using Sam Boyd Stadium.\n- Las Vegas Stadium was the working name for a domed stadium under construction in Paradise, Nevada.\n- Las Vegas Stadium was intended to host home games for the Las Vegas Raiders.\n- Las Vegas Stadium was also intended to host the UNLV Rebels football team from the University of Nevada, Las Vegas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
